---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-anchor-nav</code> is the "On this page" list of a long settings or documentation page.
  Point <code>for</code> at the element holding the content: it lists its <code>h2</code> and
  <code>h3</code> headings and marks the section being read with
  <code>aria-current="location"</code>. Pressing a link scrolls to the section (smoothly, unless
  reduced motion is on) and moves focus to its heading.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; inline-size: 100%;'>
    <wc-anchor-nav for='anchor-nav-demo' headline='On this page' style='flex: none; inline-size: 10rem;'></wc-anchor-nav>
    <wc-scroll-area style='block-size: 16rem; flex: 1;'>
      <article id='anchor-nav-demo' style='padding-inline-end: 1rem;'>
        <h2 id='anchor-profile'>Profile</h2>
        <p style='min-block-size: 10rem;'>Name, photo and the email people see.</p>
        <h3 id='anchor-photo'>Photo</h3>
        <p style='min-block-size: 8rem;'>A square image of at least 256 pixels.</p>
        <h2 id='anchor-notifications'>Notifications</h2>
        <p style='min-block-size: 10rem;'>Email, push and in-app notifications.</p>
        <h2 id='anchor-security'>Security</h2>
        <p style='min-block-size: 10rem;'>Password, passkeys and sessions.</p>
        <h2 id='anchor-danger'>Delete account</h2>
        <p>Short last sections are current at the end.</p>
      </article>
    </wc-scroll-area>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Items</h3>
<p>
  For sections that are not headings, or labels that differ from them, set <code>items</code> to
  <code>{'{ id, label, level? }'}</code> objects (<code>level</code> 2 nests under the item
  before). <code>items</code> wins over <code>for</code>.
</p>

<h3>Scroll containers, sticky and the address bar</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    The sections may scroll inside an element, such as a <code>wc-scroll-area</code>: the nav uses
    their nearest scrolling ancestor, or the element <code>scroll-container</code> selects.
  </li>
  <li>
    The nav does not stick in place by itself. In a sidebar, give it <code>position: sticky</code>
    and a <code>top</code>. When a sticky header covers the content, set
    <code>scroll-margin-top</code> on the headings.
  </li>
  <li>
    <code>update-hash</code> puts the section in the address bar with
    <code>history.replaceState()</code> when a link is pressed, without adding history entries.
  </li>
  <li>
    The nav is a <code>nav</code> landmark named "On this page", or by <code>headline</code> when
    there is one, or by <code>label</code>.
  </li>
</ul>
